id: pm-evidence-canonical-source-paths
title: Match canonical source paths in affected changed filters
description: "Fix issue #40: normalize built-in source paths across citation writes, legacy comparisons and invocation read keys; preserve source confinement and explicit refusals."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,"gh:unbraind/pm-evidence#40",paths
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:28:15.691Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T11:44:59.176Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T11:28:32.071Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed literal pre-read filtering drops equivalent legacy descriptors. Plan: one provider-aware lexical path normalizer for built-in file/JSON citation identity, comparisons and read keys; retain custom-provider identity policy and realpath/descriptor confinement. Test spelling classes, legacy records, dependency paths, cache coalescing, typed invalid operands and symlink confinement using real no-git trackers, then behavioral reverts in a disposable copy."
  "2026-11-06T11:34:31.115Z",codex-sol,"Implemented provider-aware lexical canonicalization and legacy comparison normalization; invocation caches and native source-link comparisons share it. Built-in JSON follows the same path policy; custom providers retain their prior identity contract. Added fourteen regression cases across source and built SDK, including dependencies, canonical cache coalescing, inside/outside symlinks and invalid-operand refusal. First focused run found a fixture-only optional note mismatch; corrected the assertion to use native SDK read-back as its oracle."
  "2026-11-06T11:43:55.600Z",codex-sol,"Validation: built/source spelling regressions 14/14 and pinned PM linked run 14/14 pass; existing evidence/CLI/selector suites 18/18 pass. Build, lint, typecheck, duplication (0 percent), and docstring gates pass. Behavioral reverts in a disposable source copy rebuild the SDK each time: sourceIdentity fails 13 cases; affected fails all 7 spelling cases; prepare, snapshot and Verification.read each fail the custom-provider case; writeEvidence fails the native ownership case. Every restored selection passes. Command: node test/source-paths-revert.acceptance.ts. Full release gates are delegated to CI as specified in the issue task."
  "2026-11-06T11:44:59.167Z",codex-sol,"Local strict health: history, integrity, storage, locks and merge-driver requirements pass; the only failure is the managed pm-github extension host receipt version skew (2026.11.4 versus 2026.11.5), tracked separately as pm-evidence-local-extension-skew. No dependency pin or extension configuration was changed for this fix. Fresh CI health remains authoritative for the committed tree."
